WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:38.040
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:38.310 --> 00:40.812
- Oh, no. - Wait...

3
00:41.855 --> 00:44.107
- Ms. Gong? - Mr. Dokgo.

4
00:45.025 --> 00:47.778
Why are you doing this to me?

5
00:48.862 --> 00:50.280
What do you mean?

6
00:50.614 --> 00:51.865
You started it this time.

7
00:52.240 --> 00:53.492
Mr. Dokgo.

8
00:54.534 --> 00:56.286
But you're gay.

9
00:57.496 --> 00:58.497
I'm sorry?

10
01:00.332 --> 01:01.333
I'm what?

11
01:01.667 --> 01:04.586
You're into guys.

12
01:04.920 --> 01:05.921
Who said that?

13
01:06.713 --> 01:10.384
I saw the way you were with Mr. Yun.

14
01:11.009 --> 01:12.010
"Mr. Yun"?

15
01:12.094 --> 01:13.095
You mean Ji-o?

16
01:15.555 --> 01:16.556
That's not true.

17
01:16.640 --> 01:19.768
You really don't have to hide it from me.

18
01:20.102 --> 01:21.353
In fact, I...

19
01:21.770 --> 01:24.356
I've witnessed it several times already.

20
01:24.439 --> 01:27.150
No, you're wrong. He's just a very good friend.

21
01:30.362 --> 01:31.613
I like women.

22
01:37.703 --> 01:39.663
- Really? - Do you want me to prove it?

23
01:41.039 --> 01:42.999
- What? - Then let's go to my place.

24
01:43.667 --> 01:44.793
I'm totally down.

25
01:46.712 --> 01:49.256
I don't understand.

26
01:49.339 --> 01:51.341
I can show you that I'm straight.

27
01:55.470 --> 01:57.889
You're joking.

28
02:02.436 --> 02:03.729
I'm not joking.

29
02:10.986 --> 02:12.821
What just happened

30
02:13.655 --> 02:14.865
did not happen.

31
02:18.660 --> 02:21.455
I'm sorry for the misunderstanding.

32
02:44.603 --> 02:47.230
Am I feeling relieved right now?

33
02:51.193 --> 02:52.903
You're crazy, Yeon-su.

34
02:58.867 --> 03:01.411
Let's separate.

35
03:01.495 --> 03:04.581
Don't say that, sweetheart. I just made ratatouille.

36
03:05.832 --> 03:07.709
The tomato sauce is simply the best.

37
03:08.460 --> 03:10.587
- Where did that come from? - I'm sick of this.

38
03:11.004 --> 03:13.298
I'm over 30, and people still think I'm gay.

39
03:13.381 --> 03:14.466
It happens all the time.

40
03:14.549 --> 03:17.385
You might as well just accept your fate.

41
03:17.469 --> 03:19.346
But why? Who thinks you're gay?

42
03:20.555 --> 03:21.556
Gong Yeon-su.

43
03:24.643 --> 03:26.353
- Let's separate. - You just said it was fate.

44
03:26.436 --> 03:28.230
It's time we fought against it.

45
03:28.522 --> 03:29.648
We're over 30 now.

46
03:29.731 --> 03:31.399
Cheers to our separation.

47
03:42.369 --> 03:46.832
MAKE ME TINGLE

48
03:48.500 --> 03:50.418
EPISODE 4

49
03:51.253 --> 03:53.255
For a passionate night with my girlfriend?

50
03:54.381 --> 03:55.590
We barely do it.

51
03:57.300 --> 03:59.719
I don't know. He says he's always tired.

52
04:01.429 --> 04:05.100
I want it to be a special night.

53
04:05.642 --> 04:07.894
Actually, it'd be my first experience.

54
04:07.978 --> 04:09.729
Your first time? That's pretty important.

55
04:09.813 --> 04:13.191
Sex gets boring when you do the same thing every time.

56
04:14.401 --> 04:15.735
I think it'd be fun.

57
04:15.819 --> 04:17.612
My boyfriend would love it too.

58
04:18.697 --> 04:19.739
The fun is a big part of it.

59
04:19.823 --> 04:22.450
So what should be included in the random box?

60
04:22.742 --> 04:24.160
My honest opinion?

61
04:24.244 --> 04:26.329
Well, let me think.

62
04:26.872 --> 04:29.040
- Something romantic. - Romantic?

63
04:29.124 --> 04:31.251
Something unexpected. It'd be disappointing

64
04:31.334 --> 04:32.502
to find the same old things.

65
04:32.961 --> 04:33.962
My thoughts, exactly.

66
04:35.171 --> 04:36.256
Let's open them.

67
04:40.635 --> 04:42.888
Only sex toys inside?

68
04:43.388 --> 04:45.265
A perfume and a candle?

69
04:46.308 --> 04:47.475
Our random box

70
04:48.226 --> 04:49.811
isn't a toy for kids.

71
04:50.395 --> 04:52.564
You said the fun was a part of it.

72
04:52.647 --> 04:53.940
Also, it's supposed to be eventful.

73
04:54.190 --> 04:56.526
These are too hardcore.

74
04:56.610 --> 04:57.777
Still, this won't work.

75
04:58.445 --> 04:59.863
This is 200mL.

76
05:00.196 --> 05:02.115
That means this won't work either.

77
05:02.365 --> 05:03.867
This is 250mL.

78
05:04.701 --> 05:06.161
It's necessary.

79
05:08.121 --> 05:11.541
Are you giving up on the surprise, fun, and romance?

80
05:11.625 --> 05:13.084
Efficiency is what matters most.

81
05:13.543 --> 05:15.462
It won't be fun if there's not much to it.

82
05:15.545 --> 05:18.465
But I think you're focusing a little too much on efficiency.

83
05:20.592 --> 05:22.510
Why do you think I added this?

84
05:22.886 --> 05:26.681
This lube helps reduce friction and ease the pain.

85
05:27.182 --> 05:30.435
For some people, it may be essential depending on their condition.

86
05:31.144 --> 05:33.104
The demand is surprisingly high

87
05:33.438 --> 05:34.481
and the cost is fairly low.

88
05:35.065 --> 05:37.859
It offers much more value in terms of need and efficiency

89
05:38.485 --> 05:40.904
than something like scented candles.

90
05:41.237 --> 05:44.115
Plus, the perfume and the candle aren't even our products.

91
05:44.824 --> 05:47.827
Obviously, we need to take the cost into consideration.

92
06:04.636 --> 06:07.180
I get his point about the perfume.

93
06:07.263 --> 06:09.516
But wasn't the candle a pretty good idea?

94
06:09.599 --> 06:11.393
Doesn't he get romance?

95
06:13.603 --> 06:16.648
Well, what would I expect from a guy who thinks love is

96
06:16.731 --> 06:18.441
just a reproductive urge?

97
06:19.275 --> 06:23.238
If all we care about is efficiency, why are we even making random boxes?

98
06:23.321 --> 06:25.115
We could just sell them as a bundle.

99
06:25.198 --> 06:26.282
Hey, Ms. Gong.

100
06:26.783 --> 06:29.160
Is that man the only thing on your mind?

101
06:29.953 --> 06:34.040
Gosh, you've been rattling on about him for days.

102
06:34.124 --> 06:37.419
You're seriously obsessed.

103
06:37.502 --> 06:39.629
What are you talking about? I'm not obsessed.

104
06:39.713 --> 06:41.006
What? Hey.

105
06:44.384 --> 06:46.386
Yeon-su, give it to me straight.

106
06:46.928 --> 06:48.596
Are you glad he's not gay?

107
06:48.680 --> 06:49.723
Not at all.

108
06:49.806 --> 06:52.976
It's none of my business whether he's gay or not.

109
06:53.059 --> 06:55.770
Then why the test kiss?

110
06:55.854 --> 06:57.772
What were you trying to figure out?

111
06:59.899 --> 07:00.942
Tell me.

112
07:01.568 --> 07:02.819
Say something.

113
07:05.613 --> 07:07.032
Try some of this.

114
07:11.703 --> 07:13.663
- Baek-hee. - Yes?

115
07:14.039 --> 07:15.874
So when's a good time?

116
07:16.624 --> 07:18.293
Any time works for me.

117
07:19.794 --> 07:22.338
What do old folks like us have to be busy with?

118
07:22.422 --> 07:23.506
Exactly.

119
07:23.590 --> 07:25.592
It's you young people who are busy.

120
07:26.259 --> 07:27.260
Yeon-su.

121
07:27.677 --> 07:30.013
- When's a good time for you? - Me?

122
07:30.722 --> 07:33.850
Well, I'm not sure. I have to check my schedule.

123
07:34.309 --> 07:35.518
Would he like chicken?

124
07:36.394 --> 07:38.897
Most people like chicken.

125
07:39.272 --> 07:41.107
But what is this for? Are we having guests?

126
07:41.566 --> 07:43.026
We're inviting Mr. Dokgo for a meal.

127
07:47.072 --> 07:48.698
Inviting who?

128
07:48.782 --> 07:51.409
He came all this way before, and we just let him leave.

129
07:51.493 --> 07:53.244
That's no way to treat a guest.

130
07:53.578 --> 07:54.954
Of course not.

131
07:56.831 --> 07:58.792
I'll treat him to a meal separately.

132
07:58.875 --> 08:00.460
It's just a meal.

133
08:00.752 --> 08:02.378
We'll keep it simple and make samgyetang.

134
08:02.462 --> 08:03.838
Just ask if he likes chicken.

135
08:05.423 --> 08:07.717
I'll treat him to a proper meal at a famous place

136
08:08.301 --> 08:09.594
that specializes in native chicken.

137
08:11.638 --> 08:13.473
When an elder tells you something...

138
08:14.891 --> 08:16.101
Don't argue. Just bring him.

139
08:24.484 --> 08:26.152
Okay, Grandpa.

140
08:29.656 --> 08:30.657
Invite him.

141
08:31.533 --> 08:33.118
ELECTRICAL INSPECTION POWER OUTAGE NOTICE

142
08:33.201 --> 08:35.829
This is an announcement from the management office.

143
08:35.912 --> 08:37.872
Due to an electrical inspection

144
08:37.956 --> 08:41.960
the power will be out from 7 to 7:30 p.m...

145
09:07.485 --> 09:08.987
I've been thinking.

146
09:11.030 --> 09:13.408
The candle should be included in the random box.

147
09:14.492 --> 09:16.035
I thought we were done talking about this.

148
09:16.119 --> 09:18.955
Ms. Gong still can't let go of the candle.

149
09:19.497 --> 09:21.291
It's starting again.

150
09:21.374 --> 09:24.252
Without this, the random box loses its purpose.

151
09:24.627 --> 09:27.172
I don't mind dropping the perfume, Jenga, or bath bombs

152
09:27.255 --> 09:31.176
but this candle has to stay.

153
09:31.259 --> 09:32.260
Convince me.

154
09:32.343 --> 09:35.305
Why are you so determined to keep it?

155
09:37.557 --> 09:39.309
You really don't get it, do you?

156
09:39.976 --> 09:43.897
There's one crucial thing missing from this box.

157
09:43.980 --> 09:45.815
- Which is? - Emotion.

158
09:46.107 --> 09:48.526
Something for the heart, not just the body.

159
09:48.610 --> 09:52.155
That cozy warmth and romantic mood you only get from candlelight, no?

160
09:56.784 --> 09:57.785
It's unnecessary.

161
10:00.914 --> 10:02.207
That was a hard no.

162
10:02.457 --> 10:05.043
How disappointing.

163
10:06.794 --> 10:08.421
Is she going in?

164
10:08.504 --> 10:10.089
- She is. - She's going.

165
10:15.511 --> 10:19.307
- Are you doing this on purpose? - Doing what?

166
10:20.850 --> 10:23.686
Do you not understand what I'm saying

167
10:23.770 --> 10:25.521
or are you choosing not to?

168
10:27.941 --> 10:29.442
I simply don't understand.

169
10:29.692 --> 10:31.402
Do you know why you don't?

170
10:32.195 --> 10:35.698
You're only focused on selling the mystery concept.

171
10:36.074 --> 10:37.992
You just want to fill the box

172
10:38.076 --> 10:40.495
with practical, high-performing products that have enough demand

173
10:40.578 --> 10:43.206
fit the price point, and make good business sense.

174
10:43.289 --> 10:44.457
Any problem with that?

175
10:44.916 --> 10:47.085
It sounds perfectly sensible to me.

176
10:47.168 --> 10:49.462
Why people look forward to the surprise

177
10:49.712 --> 10:51.589
what makes them smile

178
10:51.881 --> 10:54.592
or how it helps couples connect emotionally.

179
10:54.676 --> 10:56.052
You never consider these.

180
10:56.761 --> 11:00.932
To me, that candle is what defines this random box.

181
11:01.015 --> 11:05.687
It shows that this company cares about the heart, not just the body.

182
11:06.271 --> 11:08.439
Just like you analyze what satisfies people

183
11:08.523 --> 11:11.276
I analyze their emotions and consumer desires.

184
11:11.359 --> 11:13.444
At least in this field

185
11:13.528 --> 11:16.364
I know a little more than you do, Mr. Dokgo.

186
11:16.447 --> 11:19.117
Didn't my ad resonate with you enough to come find me?

187
11:19.200 --> 11:20.618
Then you should trust me.

188
11:29.460 --> 11:30.795
- What? - What?

189
11:30.878 --> 11:33.298
Why aren't you saying anything?

190
11:33.381 --> 11:35.800
You're not entirely wrong.

191
11:36.634 --> 11:39.178
Are we adding the candle then?

192
11:39.262 --> 11:42.390
You have a fair point, but I'm not completely convinced.

193
12:07.248 --> 12:08.583
I'm with you on the candle.

194
12:13.921 --> 12:19.177
Still, the company has to think about the cost of the candles

195
12:19.761 --> 12:23.139
and Dal is responsible for keeping the risk as low as possible.

196
12:25.141 --> 12:28.728
This campaign shouldn't be about playing it safe.

197
12:29.187 --> 12:34.400
It should be about shaping how consumers see this company.

198
12:35.651 --> 12:38.571
Isn't that why you put me in charge of brand marketing?

199
12:38.946 --> 12:41.657
You're right, Ms. Gong.

200
12:41.741 --> 12:44.243
Brand marketing is about shaping the image first.

201
12:45.912 --> 12:49.290
I'll talk to the candle company this week

202
12:49.374 --> 12:51.584
and see what kind of price we can work out.

203
12:53.878 --> 12:54.879
You never give up.

204
12:56.547 --> 12:57.882
We should still get off work.

205
12:58.132 --> 13:00.843
Want to grab dinner? How about some spicy udon?

206
13:01.969 --> 13:04.305
No, thank you. I still have some work left.

207
13:04.639 --> 13:06.557
Come on, just a quick bowl of udon.

208
13:07.433 --> 13:09.811
I have to get home and feed my fish too.

209
13:14.690 --> 13:15.733
Something spicy.

210
13:27.286 --> 13:30.164
Do you know the udon place we're going to?

211
13:30.248 --> 13:32.542
No, I don't. Is it far from here?

212
13:32.625 --> 13:34.127
We've been there before.

213
13:34.210 --> 13:36.170
- Really? - For a team dinner.

214
13:37.171 --> 13:38.548
They have really nice food.

215
13:48.808 --> 13:49.809
HAE, BYEOL'S MOM

216
13:49.892 --> 13:51.227
Please come this time.

217
13:51.310 --> 13:53.396
Hae and Byeol really miss you.

218
13:53.479 --> 13:54.689
I'd appreciate it.

219
14:08.494 --> 14:11.205
- Set it up here. - Yes, sir.

220
14:22.300 --> 14:23.384
Thank you.

221
14:26.429 --> 14:27.430
Thank you.

222
14:34.228 --> 14:35.313
You don't like crown daisy?

223
14:36.522 --> 14:39.567
Not really. I'm not a fan of the grassy taste.

224
14:46.240 --> 14:48.367
Mr. Yun, you seem like the type

225
14:48.868 --> 14:51.287
who eats whatever his girlfriend leaves behind

226
14:51.370 --> 14:53.080
when she's full or picky about food.

227
14:53.581 --> 14:54.582
Isn't that normal?

228
14:55.166 --> 14:57.585
No, not everyone does that.

229
14:58.628 --> 15:00.588
I see it as a privilege.

230
15:01.839 --> 15:03.883
That's something you can only do for someone you like.

231
15:05.927 --> 15:07.553
Yeah, I think you're right.

232
15:08.888 --> 15:11.307
Which one do you like more? Steamed bun or fish-shaped pastry?

233
15:11.390 --> 15:12.558
- Now? - Yes.

234
15:13.601 --> 15:14.644
Fish-shaped pastry.

235
15:14.727 --> 15:16.395
- Ramyeon or udon? - Udon.

236
15:17.271 --> 15:18.773
Got it. I'll remember that.

237
15:19.941 --> 15:21.692
- Dig in. - Bon appétit.

238
15:21.776 --> 15:22.860
Bon appétit.

239
15:30.701 --> 15:31.702
It's delicious.

240
15:35.081 --> 15:36.958
Security mode turned off.

241
15:47.885 --> 15:50.054
Everyone from Loand has also left.

242
15:50.137 --> 15:51.973
No one's inside the building.

243
15:52.056 --> 15:53.099
Roger that.

244
15:53.182 --> 15:54.725
Power will go out in five minutes.

245
16:05.611 --> 16:08.489
It's normal to have disagreements at work.

246
16:09.031 --> 16:11.534
And honestly, Dal can be a little difficult.

247
16:14.370 --> 16:15.830
I won't argue with that.

248
16:17.164 --> 16:18.666
Give him a little time.

249
16:19.208 --> 16:22.837
Dal isn't very good at opening up to people.

250
16:23.296 --> 16:26.299
He once said to me over drinks

251
16:26.924 --> 16:29.969
that there's no door handle to his heart.

252
16:30.303 --> 16:32.888
What does he mean by that?

253
16:34.056 --> 16:35.308
I guess he means it literally.

254
16:35.558 --> 16:38.019
What happens when a door is shut and there's no handle?

255
16:39.020 --> 16:42.356
No one can get in.

256
16:43.357 --> 16:44.692
But the problem is

257
16:45.526 --> 16:47.987
he can't get out either.

258
16:48.738 --> 16:53.034
That's when I started acting like a puppy around him.

259
16:53.743 --> 16:56.621
I have to keep making noise at the door

260
16:56.704 --> 16:59.165
just to get a response through the crack in the door.

261
17:16.724 --> 17:17.725
What the heck?

262
18:16.867 --> 18:18.202
A ghost!

263
18:18.994 --> 18:19.995
Get away!

264
18:20.955 --> 18:23.749
Mr. Dokgo?

265
18:32.591 --> 18:34.969
Oh, Ms. Gong?

266
18:35.678 --> 18:37.972
Are you okay?

267
18:47.857 --> 18:48.858
Yes.

268
19:06.167 --> 19:07.793
I thought you left.

269
19:07.877 --> 19:11.297
I had a few things to finish.

270
19:11.630 --> 19:13.215
I came back after dinner

271
19:13.591 --> 19:15.551
and I heard about the electrical inspection.

272
19:15.634 --> 19:17.219
So I came up to grab my bag.

273
19:18.429 --> 19:21.307
They should've given us a heads-up about the inspection.

274
19:21.557 --> 19:22.600
They did.

275
19:23.058 --> 19:24.101
Really?

276
19:24.185 --> 19:27.772
They put up the notice in the lobby and in the elevator.

277
19:27.855 --> 19:29.064
They even made announcements.

278
19:29.607 --> 19:30.608
Did they?

279
19:33.527 --> 19:35.863
Are you afraid of the dark?

280
19:37.031 --> 19:40.159
- Who said that? - Are you afraid of ghosts?

281
19:49.084 --> 19:52.630
Actually, I used to be afraid of the rain.

282
19:52.922 --> 19:54.840
I told you I didn't like the rain, right?

283
19:56.467 --> 19:58.427
You don't have to comfort me.

284
19:59.345 --> 20:01.013
It only makes me uncomfortable.

285
20:01.096 --> 20:04.934
I'm not trying to comfort you.

286
20:05.226 --> 20:06.811
It's because of the candle.

287
20:06.894 --> 20:09.980
Funny how looking at this gets me talking.

288
20:18.864 --> 20:23.911
When I was little, I once got locked in the bathroom.

289
20:23.994 --> 20:27.039
No matter how much I screamed, my parents didn't come

290
20:27.706 --> 20:29.542
because of the sound of the rain.

291
20:31.794 --> 20:34.505
It felt like the rain was swallowing my voice

292
20:35.339 --> 20:36.799
and that terrified me.

293
20:54.733 --> 20:58.737
I still don't like it, but I'm not afraid of it anymore.

294
20:59.488 --> 21:02.950
I realized what I felt back then wasn't really fear.

295
21:03.033 --> 21:05.119
It was sadness.

296
21:06.161 --> 21:08.956
Once I understood what that feeling actually was

297
21:09.039 --> 21:10.457
I felt better.

298
21:14.044 --> 21:16.255
What would it be for you, Mr. Dokgo?

299
21:17.089 --> 21:20.426
What could've been the feeling underneath the fear?

300
21:26.765 --> 21:28.767
Dad!

301
21:29.393 --> 21:31.270
Mom!

302
21:31.562 --> 21:35.608
Dad!

303
21:38.402 --> 21:39.403
Probably...

304
21:41.405 --> 21:42.406
loneliness.

305
22:12.853 --> 22:15.105
Wasn't it quite useful?

306
22:16.732 --> 22:17.775
So are you saying

307
22:18.484 --> 22:21.779
this candle made us have that cringey conversation?

308
22:21.862 --> 22:24.823
Just enough darkness, just enough light

309
22:25.824 --> 22:29.119
a little warmth, and the right mood.

310
22:29.536 --> 22:31.705
Every romance needs them.

311
22:33.582 --> 22:34.583
Was that

312
22:36.210 --> 22:37.753
romance just now?

313
22:40.589 --> 22:41.590
Sorry?

314
22:45.052 --> 22:47.137
No, I mean, what do you...

315
22:48.806 --> 22:50.766
I was referring to the random box, not us.

316
22:51.976 --> 22:55.354
Let's give random box buyers a touch of romance.

317
22:55.437 --> 22:57.189
Something like that.

318
23:00.985 --> 23:02.695
Well, the lights are back on

319
23:03.237 --> 23:05.239
so I'll be heading out.

320
23:06.323 --> 23:09.118
By the way, Mr. Dokgo...

321
23:10.077 --> 23:12.538
- I'm sure you hate samgyetang, no? - No.

322
23:13.288 --> 23:14.623
I don't hate it.

323
23:14.707 --> 23:17.584
- Any chicken allergies? - None.

324
23:18.627 --> 23:19.753
- Why? - What?

325
23:22.756 --> 23:24.633
Never mind.

326
23:24.717 --> 23:26.093
I'll be going, then.

327
24:05.424 --> 24:07.259
THANK YOU, MOM AND DAD

328
24:09.303 --> 24:11.221
DAD, MOM, HAE, ME

329
24:19.688 --> 24:21.023
- You came. - Yes.

330
24:22.816 --> 24:25.069
Girls, look who's here.

331
24:29.990 --> 24:31.450
Dal!

332
24:31.533 --> 24:32.534
Dal!

333
24:32.951 --> 24:35.621
- Come here, Hae and Byeol. - Dal!

334
24:35.954 --> 24:38.248
- There. - You finally came.

335
24:38.332 --> 24:41.543
We want to play with you, but you never come.

336
24:42.169 --> 24:45.089
I'm sorry. I'm busy all the time.

337
24:45.172 --> 24:46.173
Wait here.

338
24:48.967 --> 24:51.261
- They're for you. - Wow, it's so pretty.

339
24:51.970 --> 24:54.348
Let's open it over there.

340
24:55.599 --> 24:57.434
- He's over there. - It's so pretty!

341
25:06.151 --> 25:07.319
Happy birthday.

342
25:07.778 --> 25:10.030
Let's skip the small talk.

343
25:10.697 --> 25:12.282
You've had enough fun.

344
25:12.825 --> 25:14.451
Come back to the company now.

345
25:14.535 --> 25:16.912
You've dragged my name through the mud enough.

346
25:17.955 --> 25:18.997
I'm not done having fun yet.

347
25:19.081 --> 25:20.457
You insolent brat.

348
25:20.999 --> 25:22.626
You can't get investors

349
25:22.709 --> 25:24.169
and you can't even market it properly.

350
25:24.419 --> 25:25.879
And you still call that a business?

351
25:25.963 --> 25:27.714
You seem invested in my company.

352
25:27.798 --> 25:30.008
It's stupid to cling to something that's not working.

353
25:30.384 --> 25:33.512
If you're a man, you should have the guts to walk away!

354
25:33.595 --> 25:35.430
- Like you did with your marriage? - What?

355
25:35.514 --> 25:38.892
I may lack your decisiveness, but endurance is one thing I've got.

356
25:39.143 --> 25:40.727
I'll play this out for now.

357
25:40.978 --> 25:42.771
Let's talk again around your 60th birthday.

358
25:43.147 --> 25:45.816
Who on earth did you get that stubborn streak from?

359
25:45.899 --> 25:48.443
I hate to admit it, but the stubbornness, the arrogance

360
25:48.527 --> 25:49.736
and even the womanizing...

361
25:50.320 --> 25:51.363
I got it all from you.

362
25:53.282 --> 25:54.491
I'll be off now.

363
26:07.462 --> 26:09.631
Oh, seriously?

364
26:09.965 --> 26:11.425
We should air this place out.

365
26:12.593 --> 26:16.180
Do you know how funny you looked eating that cake?

366
26:18.682 --> 26:19.933
Today was so much fun.

367
26:20.017 --> 26:22.519
Our shots were really on point...

368
26:25.355 --> 26:26.690
- Are you okay? - Yeah.

369
26:52.257 --> 26:53.800
- Yes? - So?

370
26:54.259 --> 26:55.969
When are you visiting her family again?

371
26:56.345 --> 26:59.389
I heard they took quite a liking to you.

372
27:05.103 --> 27:07.022
I'm home.

373
27:09.274 --> 27:10.275
Wait.

374
27:11.401 --> 27:13.111
Did you ask him when he's available?

375
27:13.570 --> 27:14.655
For what?

376
27:14.738 --> 27:15.989
I'm talking about Mr. Dokgo.

377
27:16.073 --> 27:18.033
Mom, why would you...

378
27:18.116 --> 27:19.910
I said I'll treat him myself.

379
27:19.993 --> 27:20.994
Just invite him.

380
27:21.495 --> 27:23.247
Not happening.

381
27:23.789 --> 27:25.666
Do you know who your grandma called?

382
27:26.083 --> 27:27.084
Your ninth-degree relative.

383
27:27.709 --> 27:29.461
What about my ninth-degree relative?

384
27:29.544 --> 27:30.587
Don't you remember?

385
27:30.921 --> 27:32.589
He set you up with Mr. Dokgo.

386
27:34.591 --> 27:36.718
- What do I do? - You know what to do.

387
27:56.113 --> 27:58.240
The candle's officially in!

388
27:59.908 --> 28:02.619
- Is this our final version? - Yes.

389
28:04.371 --> 28:05.372
USER GUIDE

390
28:05.664 --> 28:07.666
Min-hyung, are you good with coding?

391
28:07.749 --> 28:09.501
You bet I am. Why?

392
28:10.002 --> 28:13.797
Is it okay if we add one last thing?

393
28:14.381 --> 28:16.425
But we don't have any space left.

394
28:16.508 --> 28:17.968
Oh, that's not necessary.

395
28:18.510 --> 28:20.012
This paper will do.

396
28:21.388 --> 28:22.597
We can make a QR code

397
28:22.681 --> 28:26.393
and pair the random box with a matching playlist.

398
28:26.977 --> 28:27.978
A playlist?

399
28:28.061 --> 28:31.523
Lighting and music are what shape the mood of a space.

400
28:32.107 --> 28:35.235
If we link it to the user guide and the review page

401
28:35.319 --> 28:37.195
it'll be easier to access everything.

402
28:38.322 --> 28:39.865
That'd be great for collecting reviews.

403
28:40.115 --> 28:43.118
We could also add a detailed survey and star ratings.

404
28:43.785 --> 28:47.122
Finally, I should put my skills to use.

405
28:47.914 --> 28:51.543
- All right, Min-hyung. Go all out. - Okay.

406
28:51.626 --> 28:53.128
- You've got this! - You've got this!

407
28:53.879 --> 28:54.963
Show us!

408
29:15.275 --> 29:17.611
Why did you include the candle?

409
29:17.694 --> 29:19.363
You wouldn't give it up.

410
29:20.864 --> 29:24.076
I'll light the candle again if you're not honest with me.

411
29:29.706 --> 29:31.833
The power went out at the right moment

412
29:32.376 --> 29:34.169
and you showed up at the right moment.

413
29:35.295 --> 29:37.506
I happened to be afraid of the dark

414
29:38.590 --> 29:40.634
and you brought up your story about the rain.

415
29:40.717 --> 29:44.721
And at the center of it all was just one little scented candle.

416
29:45.806 --> 29:47.516
I thought it wouldn't be so bad...

417
29:49.851 --> 29:52.104
if one candle from a random box

418
29:52.646 --> 29:54.773
could find its way into someone's little coincidences

419
29:54.856 --> 29:56.650
be lit in the middle of an ordinary moment

420
29:57.025 --> 30:00.487
and draw out feelings that help two people open up to each other.

421
30:00.821 --> 30:02.489
"I liked our conversation that night."

422
30:04.825 --> 30:07.786
You took the long way around to say that.

423
30:12.082 --> 30:15.210
But why did you ask about samgyetang?

424
30:15.293 --> 30:16.294
What?

425
30:18.839 --> 30:20.507
Just because.

426
30:21.633 --> 30:23.677
It was just a random question.

427
30:27.013 --> 30:31.351
In fact, my grandpa told me to invite someone.

428
30:33.311 --> 30:35.313
- Invite who? - You, my blind date.

429
30:37.899 --> 30:39.359
- So? - Well...

430
30:39.443 --> 30:40.694
I just don't think it's right.

431
30:41.194 --> 30:43.488
I keep delaying the date, but...

432
30:43.572 --> 30:45.782
Just tell him no instead of dragging it out.

433
30:45.866 --> 30:47.409
You can't even push back that much?

434
30:48.118 --> 30:50.078
You've seen what my family's like.

435
30:50.162 --> 30:53.248
Grandpa's word is absolute. I can't defy him.

436
30:53.623 --> 30:55.250
I can't push back.

437
31:00.380 --> 31:01.965
So I was wondering...

438
31:03.300 --> 31:06.511
Could you come in person

439
31:06.595 --> 31:08.430
and turn him down for me?

440
31:08.513 --> 31:09.514
No.

441
31:10.640 --> 31:11.892
Oh, I see.

442
31:12.767 --> 31:13.768
Absolutely.

443
31:14.269 --> 31:16.062
I'm sure you wouldn't want to.

444
31:21.401 --> 31:24.946
Actually, that was a selfish request.

445
31:25.030 --> 31:27.282
Forget I asked.

446
31:27.365 --> 31:28.617
I'll find a way...

447
31:30.285 --> 31:31.620
to deal with it on my own.

448
31:51.014 --> 31:52.140
I'm crazy.

449
31:52.224 --> 31:54.643
Why did I ask him to do that?

450
31:55.185 --> 31:58.688
I let my guard down fast over one little candle.

451
32:01.399 --> 32:02.400
Ms. Gong.

452
32:03.568 --> 32:06.279
Mr. Yun, did you go somewhere?

453
32:07.489 --> 32:09.491
Ta-da. I did some fishing.

454
32:09.950 --> 32:12.202
It took me ages to find a stall in this fall weather.

455
32:15.372 --> 32:17.207
You prefer fish-shaped pastries to steamed buns.

456
32:17.290 --> 32:19.084
See how I left the bag open?

457
32:19.167 --> 32:20.335
That's so they wouldn't get soggy.

458
32:24.464 --> 32:26.508
Wait, are you a custard person, not a red bean one?

459
32:26.758 --> 32:27.801
I can run back to grab those.

460
32:28.301 --> 32:29.719
No, it's okay.

461
32:30.637 --> 32:31.638
I like both.

462
32:34.766 --> 32:35.767
Have some.

463
32:36.726 --> 32:37.727
Thanks.

464
32:40.564 --> 32:41.565
Cheers.

465
32:45.110 --> 32:46.111
Oh, it's hot.

466
32:52.325 --> 32:55.036
There's nothing like this when it's hot and fresh.

467
32:58.957 --> 33:00.875
Hey, Dal. You're still here.

468
33:02.085 --> 33:03.753
- Would you like one? - I'm good.

469
33:03.837 --> 33:04.879
I should get dinner.

470
33:06.131 --> 33:07.215
Let's continue where we left off.

471
33:08.758 --> 33:10.218
- Sorry? - Let's grab dinner.

472
33:20.687 --> 33:22.439
- Enjoy. - Thank you.

473
33:42.083 --> 33:43.460
I'll get straight to the point.

474
33:44.210 --> 33:46.463
Do you really need me to turn him down?

475
33:47.797 --> 33:50.592
I told you I'd handle it myself.

476
33:50.675 --> 33:52.093
You don't need to worry about it.

477
33:52.177 --> 33:53.511
Let me put it differently.

478
33:54.679 --> 33:56.389
Have you ever, even once

479
33:56.640 --> 33:58.933
wanted to break one of the jars in the yard?

480
34:00.435 --> 34:02.312
No, not really.

481
34:03.271 --> 34:05.148
Okay, I'll help you with that.

482
34:06.232 --> 34:09.694
First, think of something the elders would disapprove of.

483
34:10.070 --> 34:12.906
Then we'll come up with a specific plan.

484
34:19.329 --> 34:21.581
We've got so much work. I love it.

485
35:01.287 --> 35:03.206
Anything other than picky eating?

486
35:03.748 --> 35:04.749
Why?

487
35:04.833 --> 35:07.252
I used to get in so much trouble for being a picky eater.

488
35:07.335 --> 35:10.505
Because I bet your mother is a great cook.

489
35:15.343 --> 35:17.387
Let's be upfront about your job.

490
35:17.887 --> 35:18.930
Sounds good.

491
35:19.013 --> 35:20.682
But you can't mention me.

492
35:20.765 --> 35:23.143
Don't worry about that. Anything else?

493
35:25.979 --> 35:29.441
He has one thing he values above all else.

494
35:31.359 --> 35:33.862
"A man should be devoted to his family

495
35:35.029 --> 35:36.072
and carry on the family line.

496
35:36.489 --> 35:38.908
A woman should obey her husband

497
35:38.992 --> 35:40.368
and bear children to continue that line."

498
35:48.042 --> 35:49.753
That's quite intense, right?

499
35:50.295 --> 35:51.838
Should we think of something less wild?

500
35:52.088 --> 35:54.174
No, it's fine. I can take it.

501
35:56.718 --> 35:58.553
So when's the date?

502
35:58.636 --> 35:59.679
This Saturday.

503
35:59.763 --> 36:01.389
- The time? - At 12 p.m.

504
36:01.765 --> 36:04.225
Try coming 20 or 30 minutes late.

505
36:04.684 --> 36:07.854
My grandpa absolutely hates tardiness.

506
36:08.104 --> 36:10.482
Got it. I'll take note.

507
36:29.000 --> 36:30.627
The call cannot be connected...

508
36:32.629 --> 36:34.047
What's going on?

509
36:34.130 --> 36:35.381
Why isn't she picking up?

510
36:36.758 --> 36:38.468
CALL LOG

511
36:38.551 --> 36:39.677
MY SI-EUN

512
36:39.761 --> 36:42.180
- It's pretty obvious. - I agree.

513
36:44.098 --> 36:46.351
But where did Si-eun go?

514
36:46.434 --> 36:47.685
NAM-SU

515
36:47.769 --> 36:49.437
I think she went to the bathroom.

516
37:16.923 --> 37:17.924
He should be here soon, right?

517
37:20.593 --> 37:22.303
Oh, right. Baek-hee.

518
37:23.012 --> 37:24.931
Bring out the seokbakji and green onion kimchi

519
37:25.014 --> 37:26.349
we made last week.

520
37:26.432 --> 37:27.934
- Yes, Mother. - All right.

521
37:30.645 --> 37:32.814
Wasn't he supposed to be here by noon?

522
37:33.189 --> 37:34.691
There's a lot of traffic these days.

523
37:35.149 --> 37:36.484
Don't be so impatient.

524
37:36.568 --> 37:37.569
Okay.

525
37:39.904 --> 37:41.489
Should we bring out some ginseng liquor too?

526
37:41.906 --> 37:43.449
I wonder if he drinks.

527
37:48.538 --> 37:50.081
You're earlier than I expected.

528
37:50.164 --> 37:52.208
Well, it just worked out that way.

529
37:54.919 --> 37:57.088
- Shall we? - Not yet.

530
37:57.380 --> 37:59.090
It's only 15 minutes late.

531
38:00.091 --> 38:01.926
Oh, I see.

532
38:05.638 --> 38:07.348
Good afternoon.

533
38:07.849 --> 38:09.309
Are you getting married?

534
38:10.143 --> 38:11.144
Oh, my.

535
38:11.519 --> 38:13.730
You used to be tiny, and now you're getting married.

536
38:15.023 --> 38:17.066
- Bye. - Did the second child

537
38:17.150 --> 38:18.985
in her family become a civil servant yet?

538
38:19.068 --> 38:20.486
I don't think so.

539
38:30.705 --> 38:32.790
You look too neat.

540
38:33.499 --> 38:35.752
- Excuse me for a moment. - Okay.

541
38:43.384 --> 38:44.844
This will do.

542
38:46.804 --> 38:49.265
- Oh, my word. - Should I give her a call?

543
38:49.349 --> 38:51.142
Leave her be. She'll get here.

544
38:51.935 --> 38:52.936
Let's go in.

545
39:12.789 --> 39:13.998
We're here!

546
39:14.832 --> 39:16.167
Oh, they're here.

547
39:16.834 --> 39:18.044
Here they are.

548
39:35.520 --> 39:37.355
I hope it's to your taste.

549
39:38.272 --> 39:39.315
It's delicious, ma'am.

550
39:39.691 --> 39:41.776
I also loved the cheonggukjang you made last time.

551
39:41.859 --> 39:43.695
You're such a great cook.

552
39:43.778 --> 39:46.030
Oh, aren't you sweet?

553
39:46.614 --> 39:48.157
I'll make it for you again sometime.

554
39:49.534 --> 39:52.453
- What do you like? - I eat pretty much anything.

555
39:56.374 --> 39:57.417
(Don't forget.)

556
39:59.335 --> 40:02.505
As for chicken, I prefer it boiled like baeksuk.

557
40:02.588 --> 40:05.258
And I only eat tender cuts of beef like tenderloin.

558
40:06.592 --> 40:07.844
He's got refined tastes.

559
40:08.970 --> 40:11.431
Oh, I can't eat shellfish.

560
40:11.514 --> 40:12.765
I'm allergic.

561
40:14.308 --> 40:16.853
Shrimp too. I'm allergic to that as well.

562
40:17.228 --> 40:18.479
Aside from that, I'm not picky at all.

563
40:20.940 --> 40:23.151
Oh, right. I don't like eggplant.

564
40:23.860 --> 40:25.695
It's way too soft and mushy.

565
40:26.404 --> 40:29.907
I guess growing up privileged made him a picky eater.

566
40:29.991 --> 40:32.493
Times are good now, so people can afford to be picky.

567
40:32.577 --> 40:35.204
Back when we barely had enough to eat

568
40:35.288 --> 40:36.539
nobody could afford to be picky.

569
40:36.831 --> 40:39.375
We ate whatever we could get our hands on

570
40:39.876 --> 40:41.002
even tree bark boiled in water.

571
40:42.003 --> 40:43.921
You're absolutely right

572
40:44.422 --> 40:46.674
but food that doesn't agree with your body

573
40:46.758 --> 40:48.134
can do more harm than good.

574
40:51.804 --> 40:55.892
So what was it you said your company does? Toys?

575
40:55.975 --> 40:58.019
Or was it exercise equipment?

576
41:01.272 --> 41:04.817
To be more precise, we work in both areas.

577
41:05.193 --> 41:06.903
- Both areas? - Yes.

578
41:08.654 --> 41:09.989
We make sex toys.

579
41:19.832 --> 41:21.250
What toys?

580
41:21.334 --> 41:23.878
Snack toys?

581
41:24.170 --> 41:26.047
No, ma'am. It's "sex."

582
41:28.174 --> 41:29.217
Sex toys.

583
41:29.383 --> 41:32.220
Put simply, you can think of them as adult products.

584
41:32.512 --> 41:35.973
We import, make, and sell a wide range of adult products.

585
41:36.265 --> 41:38.810
It suits my personality well, so I enjoy what I do.

586
41:39.102 --> 41:40.311
You said it was a toy company.

587
41:40.770 --> 41:41.854
They are toys, sir.

588
41:42.188 --> 41:44.148
Kids play with toys

589
41:44.232 --> 41:47.276
for fun, comfort, and emotional satisfaction.

590
41:47.777 --> 41:48.945
It's no different for adults.

591
41:49.529 --> 41:52.073
These are simply toys for adults.

592
41:52.323 --> 41:56.744
Well, times have changed a lot.

593
41:57.203 --> 42:01.999
Maybe it's just an area that older folks like us don't quite get.

594
42:02.625 --> 42:04.168
You're very open-minded.

595
42:04.710 --> 42:06.629
Most people tend to have prejudices about it.

596
42:06.712 --> 42:08.339
Oh, no prejudice at all.

597
42:08.422 --> 42:09.757
Well, okay.

598
42:18.766 --> 42:22.937
I hear your father runs quite a large business.

599
42:23.271 --> 42:25.523
Do you plan to work with him someday?

600
42:26.524 --> 42:29.944
My father would like that, but I have no intention of doing so.

601
42:30.361 --> 42:32.947
I'm genuinely passionate about my business.

602
42:33.239 --> 42:36.576
Even so, if you get married and have kids

603
42:36.659 --> 42:39.162
shouldn't you have a respectable job as a parent?

604
42:40.204 --> 42:43.124
Thankfully, I won't have to worry about that either.

605
42:43.583 --> 42:45.877
I'm azoospermic.

606
42:46.919 --> 42:50.298
So I probably won't ever have children of my own.

607
42:52.800 --> 42:54.510
But what I'm really grateful for

608
42:54.594 --> 42:56.888
is that I have younger twin sisters I absolutely adore.

609
42:57.138 --> 42:58.723
My father is getting older

610
42:58.806 --> 43:01.184
so I plan to raise them as if they were my own.

611
43:06.606 --> 43:09.692
I'm perfectly functional in every other way as a man

612
43:09.775 --> 43:11.068
so that's a relief.

613
43:18.910 --> 43:23.247
I mean, except for that, he's practically perfect.

614
43:29.253 --> 43:30.421
I'll pour your drink, sir.

615
43:41.224 --> 43:44.227
I wish you nothing but the best for the future.

616
43:45.436 --> 43:46.437
Thank you, sir.

617
43:54.320 --> 43:55.905
Thank you for today.

618
43:58.199 --> 44:01.661
I don't know if I should be grateful for this, but I am.

619
44:01.744 --> 44:03.621
So thank you.

620
44:04.914 --> 44:05.915
Is that all?

621
44:06.958 --> 44:08.125
Honestly...

622
44:09.126 --> 44:10.628
I'm nervous about it.

623
44:11.545 --> 44:12.964
And a little scared.

624
44:13.047 --> 44:14.465
Not even a little cathartic?

625
44:18.970 --> 44:20.763
This was actually my first time.

626
44:21.555 --> 44:23.849
I've never thrown the elders off like that before

627
44:23.933 --> 44:26.519
or messed up their plans.

628
44:28.854 --> 44:31.232
Your marriage, your partner's career

629
44:31.315 --> 44:33.442
their qualifications, and having children...

630
44:33.859 --> 44:37.113
They planned it all without your consent.

631
44:37.697 --> 44:39.323
You don't need to feel guilty.

632
44:42.994 --> 44:44.537
Is this what she meant?

633
44:46.205 --> 44:48.791
My aunt said she shouted for joy outside the courthouse

634
44:49.166 --> 44:51.919
the day she filed for divorce.

635
44:52.503 --> 44:56.465
She said making such a huge, life-changing decision for herself

636
44:56.549 --> 44:58.134
felt exhilarating.

637
44:58.718 --> 45:02.263
I'm starting to understand how she felt.

638
45:02.972 --> 45:07.727
For the first time, I felt this sense of freedom.

639
45:09.812 --> 45:10.938
That's good.

640
45:12.815 --> 45:16.027
You're honest and decisive, Ms. Gong.

641
45:16.944 --> 45:19.196
Live your own life the way you'd market it.

642
45:20.031 --> 45:21.407
That's the way to go.

643
45:24.618 --> 45:26.829
Are you cheering me on right now?

644
45:26.912 --> 45:28.998
No, that was advice in disguise.

645
45:30.166 --> 45:32.543
But hear it however you like.

646
45:34.295 --> 45:37.173
I'm saying don't lose that bold, slightly crazy side of you.

647
45:39.175 --> 45:41.552
No matter where you are.

648
45:44.096 --> 45:46.724
This man is always testing me.

649
45:46.807 --> 45:49.727
Anyway, that's all sorted out.

650
45:50.811 --> 45:53.147
We don't have to be tied together as former blind dates anymore.

651
45:53.814 --> 45:56.442
And whatever connection our families had is over too.

652
45:57.234 --> 45:59.987
We're completely out of each other's personal lives now.

653
46:00.696 --> 46:04.533
So from here on out, it's strictly business between us.

654
46:05.868 --> 46:10.039
He barges in and shakes the handle to my heart without warning.

655
46:17.630 --> 46:20.049
You should go in. I'll see you at the office.

656
46:32.561 --> 46:33.562
Mr. Dokgo.

657
46:52.665 --> 46:55.543
Would you like to go on a date with me?

658
47:10.683 --> 47:14.603
Our personal boundaries have expanded.

659
47:16.147 --> 47:20.151
MAKE ME TINGLE

660
47:36.000 --> 47:37.710
That's big trouble.

661
47:38.544 --> 47:40.004
Oh, my goodness.

662
47:56.937 --> 47:58.189
HORIZON IT GETS CLEARER AS IT GOES FARTHER...

663
47:58.272 --> 47:59.815
RANDOM BOX

664
47:59.899 --> 48:01.442
IF I GET LOST, SO DOES THE BRAND!

665
48:05.446 --> 48:08.115
LOVE ISN'T ABOUT UNDERSTANDING IT'S ABOUT ACCEPTANCE...

666
49:52.011 --> 49:54.013
Subtitles by Cherry Park
